# Line-ending policy.
#
# This project builds and runs inside Linux containers. Shell scripts — above
# all the API container's entrypoint — MUST keep LF endings. Without this, a
# Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true rewrites them to CRLF; the shebang
# then becomes "#!/bin/sh\r" and the container dies at startup with:
#
#   exec /app/packages/api/entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory
#
# See https://github.com/fabriziosalmi/nis2-public/issues/202
*.sh        text eol=lf
entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf

# Let Git normalise text files, but never touch known binaries.
*           text=auto
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary
*.svg       text
*.pdf       binary
*.mp4       binary
*.woff      binary
*.woff2     binary
*.ttf       binary
